      "side": 1,
      "message": "If fuzzing, we should never touch anything from the vendor/product/system partitions. All dependent shared libraries (even transient dependencies) are re-exported to the data partition with the target.\n\nThe issue I\u0027m trying to highlight here is that if:\n 1. You build your entire platform with sanitizer coverage (SANITIZE_TARGET\u003dfuzzer make droid), which is perhaps not a useful configuration anyway, and\n 2. There is a shared library that\u0027s in two different partitions that are expected to cross over, e.g:\n\n     /alpha/foo.so has DT_NEEDED on bar.so\n     ... but expects the bar.so from /bravo/bar.so, and not\n     /alpha/bar.so (which I assume doesn\u0027t ever happen), then this change will have an adverse effect.",
